hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2782","Narrated to us Saʿīd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbdil-Ḥakam: narrated to us Ḥafṣ—meaning ibn ʿUmar al-ʿAdanī: narrated to us Yazīd ibn Mulaik al-ʿAdanī: narrated to us Abū Ṭufail (RA), who said:\n*\I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performing Tawāf around the House upon his camel or riding beast"," while he was touching the Corner [al-Rukn al-Yamānī] with his staff [miḥjan]"," and then kissing the tip of the staff.\""*\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
"2783","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Sa‘īd al-Dārimī: narrated to us Abū ‘Āṣim, on the authority of Abū Kharrbūdh, who said: Abū al-Ṭufayl narrated to me, saying:\n“I saw the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) circumambulating the House upon his riding animal, and he would touch the Corners with his staff. He said: ‘And I saw him kiss the end of the staff, then he went out to al-Ṣafā and circumambulated upon his riding animal.’”\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
